                <pb facs="0448" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg340"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Lord Stanley, of Preston.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-11"><hi rendition="#italic">January 11,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: With reference to your excellency’s
                    dispatch No. 76 of November 25, I have the honor to inclose a copy of a note,
                    which I have received from Mr. Foster, containing observations on the minute of
                    council in regard to the Welland Canal toll controversy which accompanied your
                    excellency’s above mentioned dispatch.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
